---
title: Reference
summary: Every setting Vesper reads, with its default, and the vesper command.
---

These pages list every setting in one place, with its exact name and default. The guides explain when you'd want each one; come here when you know what you want and need the details.

Vesper reads two files of yours. `vesper()` in `astro.config.mjs` sets up the integration: the studio's deployment, search, the build's accessibility check, and publishing with GitHub or the cloud. `vesper.config.ts` says how the studio presents your collections and where their entries live on the site. Neither holds field definitions: those stay in `src/content.config.ts`.
